---
import ConversionBand from '@components/ConversionBand.astro';
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Mission"
  description="ArchUnit’s mission is to make software architecture executable, understandable, and native to the way engineering teams work."
  canonicalPath="/mission/"
>
  <section class="statement-hero">
    <div class="shell statement-hero__inner">
      <p class="hero-kicker">Our mission</p>
      <h1>Make architecture a capability every team can exercise.</h1>
      <p>
        Software structure should not depend on someone remembering a diagram. It should remain
        visible, testable, and open to deliberate change.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="statement-body-section">
    <div class="shell statement-body-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Why this matters</p>
        <h2>Architecture is the accumulated effect of everyday decisions.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          Most structural decline is not caused by one dramatic choice. It comes from thousands of
          reasonable local changes that no longer add up to the system teams intended to build.
        </p>
        <p>
          We build ArchUnit so engineers can state the boundaries that matter, evaluate them with
          real source code, and receive feedback while the context for a change is still present.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our aim is not to freeze design. It is to make change explicit. A useful architecture rule
          creates a shared point of discussion, a testable expectation, and a record of when a team
          chooses a different direction.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mission-pillars-section">
    <div class="shell mission-pillars-grid">
      <article>
        <span>01</span>
        <h2>Visible</h2>
        <p>Teams can inspect the graph, rule, and evidence.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>02</span>
        <h2>Native</h2>
        <p>The API belongs in the language and test culture around it.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>03</span>
        <h2>Actionable</h2>
        <p>A failure explains the decision and the path back to a healthy state.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>04</span>
        <h2>Adaptable</h2>
        <p>Rules support deliberate evolution rather than preserving yesterday forever.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ConversionBand
    eyebrow="The work ahead"
    title="A shared architecture language, expressed natively."
    copy="Explore the principles that guide our decisions and the people translating them across ecosystems."
    primaryLabel="Our principles"
    primaryHref="/principles/"
    secondaryLabel="Meet the team"
    secondaryHref="/team/"
  />
</BaseLayout>
